-- title:
--   Two-chart glued model: proper, smooth, closed points are places
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be an infinite perfect field and $L$ a field extension of $K$ (both in the same universe), and let $t \in L$ be a nonzero element that is transcendental over $K$ and such that $L$ is finite-dimensional and separable over the intermediate field $K\langle t\rangle = K(t)$. Write $\mathrm{chartRing}\,K\,S$ for the subalgebra of elements of $L$ integral over the $K$-subalgebra generated by a subset $S \subseteq L$, and let `glued K t` be the scheme obtained as the pushout of $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the two charts $\mathrm{chartRing}\,K\,\{t\}$ and $\mathrm{chartRing}\,K\,\{t^{-1}\}$ along $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the overlap chart $\mathrm{chartRing}\,K\,\{t,t^{-1}\}$, with `gluedToBase K t` the induced morphism to $\operatorname{Spec} K$ descended from the two structure morphisms. The assertion is the conjunction of four statements: (1) `gluedToBase K t` is proper; (2) it is smooth of relative dimension $1$; (3) there is a bijection $P$ from the closed points of `glued K t` to the places of $L/K$, a place being a valuation subring of $L$ containing the image of $K$, different from $L$ itself, and a principal ideal ring, such that for every closed point $x$ the image of the stalk at $x$ inside $L$ — taken along the map from the stalk to the function field of `glued K t` followed by the inverse of the ring isomorphism `gluedFunctionFieldEquiv K t` $: L \simeq$ (function field) — is exactly the underlying subring of the valuation ring of $P x$; and (4) every finite set of points of `glued K t` is contained in some affine open subset. These are the conditions assembled by the structure `CurveModel`, apart from the compatibility of the function field identification with the structure map from $K$.
--
--   This is the classical statement that the normal proper model of a one-variable function field $L/K$ is a smooth proper curve whose closed points correspond to the places of $L/K$, here in the characteristic-free form obtained from the explicit two-chart construction over an arbitrary infinite perfect base field. It is used to produce a `CurveModel` for such function fields (as in `exists_curveModel_ratFunc` and `nonempty_of_perfectField`) and thence in the divisor-class-group results such as [`AlgebraicCurve.Pic0.exists_nsmul_eq_of_charP`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.Pic0.exists_nsmul_eq_of_charP).
